{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"2a05a6fa89a63666","name":"card_event_exhaust_all_options","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BloodIron/events/card_event_exhaust_all_options","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"EXHAUST ALL OPTIONS","text":"Pin target unit and adjacent units. Pin units deployed and added by the enemy next turn.","flavorText":"The Battle of Bataan was fought from January 7th to April 9th, 1942 and was a major battle opposing the Japanese to the US and Filipino forces during the early stages of WWII in the Pacific Theater. It took place on the Bataan Peninsula in the Philippines and was part of the broader Japanese invasion of the Philippines. Following the attack on Pearl Harbor, Japanese forces advanced across Southeast Asia, and by December 1941, they were pressing into the Philippines. American and Filipino forces, commanded by General Douglas MacArthur and later by Major General Edward P. King, retreated to the Bataan Peninsula, where they established defensive positions. Outnumbered, outgunned, and suffering from severe shortages of food, medicine, and supplies, the defenders fought a grueling, three-month-long battle against the Japanese. Despite their valiant efforts, the Allied forces were overwhelmed by the superior Japanese troops. On April 9th, 1942, Major General King was forced to surrender Bataan, marking one of the largest surrenders in US military history. Around 76,000 American and Filipino soldiers were captured and subjected to the infamous Bataan Death March, during which thousands of prisoners died from exhaustion, disease, and brutal treatment by their captors.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_exhaust_all_options","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_exhaust_all_options_title","SourceString":"EXHAUST ALL OPTIONS","LocalizedString":"EXHAUST ALL OPTIONS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_exhaust_all_options_text","SourceString":"Pin target unit and adjacent units. Pin units deployed and added by the enemy next turn.","LocalizedString":"Pin target unit and adjacent units. Pin units deployed and added by the enemy next turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_exhaust_all_options_history","SourceString":"The Battle of Bataan was fought from January 7th to April 9th, 1942 and was a major battle opposing the Japanese to the US and Filipino forces during the early stages of WWII in the Pacific Theater. It took place on the Bataan Peninsula in the Philippines and was part of the broader Japanese invasion of the Philippines. Following the attack on Pearl Harbor, Japanese forces advanced across Southeast Asia, and by December 1941, they were pressing into the Philippines. American and Filipino forces, commanded by General Douglas MacArthur and later by Major General Edward P. King, retreated to the Bataan Peninsula, where they established defensive positions. Outnumbered, outgunned, and suffering from severe shortages of food, medicine, and supplies, the defenders fought a grueling, three-month-long battle against the Japanese. Despite their valiant efforts, the Allied forces were overwhelmed by the superior Japanese troops. On April 9th, 1942, Major General King was forced to surrender Bataan, marking one of the largest surrenders in US military history. Around 76,000 American and Filipino soldiers were captured and subjected to the infamous Bataan Death March, during which thousands of prisoners died from exhaustion, disease, and brutal treatment by their captors.","LocalizedString":"The Battle of Bataan was fought from January 7th to April 9th, 1942 and was a major battle opposing the Japanese to the US and Filipino forces during the early stages of WWII in the Pacific Theater. It took place on the Bataan Peninsula in the Philippines and was part of the broader Japanese invasion of the Philippines. Following the attack on Pearl Harbor, Japanese forces advanced across Southeast Asia, and by December 1941, they were pressing into the Philippines. American and Filipino forces, commanded by General Douglas MacArthur and later by Major General Edward P. King, retreated to the Bataan Peninsula, where they established defensive positions. Outnumbered, outgunned, and suffering from severe shortages of food, medicine, and supplies, the defenders fought a grueling, three-month-long battle against the Japanese. Despite their valiant efforts, the Allied forces were overwhelmed by the superior Japanese troops. On April 9th, 1942, Major General King was forced to surrender Bataan, marking one of the largest surrenders in US military history. Around 76,000 American and Filipino soldiers were captured and subjected to the infamous Bataan Death March, during which thousands of prisoners died from exhaustion, disease, and brutal treatment by their captors."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Pin"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Winter_2024/t_exhaust_all_options.t_exhaust_all_options","SubPathString":""},"artist":"1518 Studios","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/EXHAUST_ALL_OPTIONS.EXHAUST_ALL_OPTIONS","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":395.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_exhaust_all_options_photo","SourceString":"Japanese tanks and infantry advancing through the Bataan jungle, 1942.","LocalizedString":"Japanese tanks and infa